    {
      "content": "You are an offline code repair agent. Solve only the task below. The workspace contains the pinned source tree; tool access is allowlisted. Search candidate-visible source, then inspect a narrow range using read_lines. Use read_lines to obtain a one-time lease, then call replace_lines_transactional with the complete replacement, and the required explicit normalization choice. The controller assembles and parses the entire Python file before writing it; a syntax-invalid proposal is rejected without changing the candidate. Only choose a fence or newline normalization when the raw replacement actually needs that exact mechanical transformation. Semantic code is never inferred or repaired by the controller. After a committed edit, call run_public_tests and use its feedback before finishing. Allowed source paths: src/transformers/generation/utils.py. Search candidate-visible source first; the search tool searches only these paths. Do not invent paths. The workspace is already prepared; never ask for a workspace path, more information, or permission. The external grader is hidden. Do not describe a fix without applying it. Call finish only after changing a source file. After changing source, call run_public_tests; read its output and repair failures. The public checks are immutable. Call finish only after the public smoke test passes. You have a limited tool budget; each assistant turn before finish must call a tool. TASK:\n# Repair encoder-side generation penalties for missing source IDs\n\nWhen a seq2seq model is called with precomputed `encoder_outputs` but without source `input_ids`, generation creates dummy negative sentinel IDs. The encoder repetition and no-repeat-ngram processors must not treat those sentinels as real source tokens. They should be skipped, and the existing missing-input warnings should be emitted. When valid `input_ids` are supplied, preserve both processors without that warning. Limit the repair to `src/transformers/generation/utils.py`.\n\nThe public regression runs a randomly initialized local T5 model and requires generation to complete for both constraints. No model weights or network access are used by the test.",
